WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.604
Here's the book's sequence
applied to moving

2
00:00:03.604 --> 00:00:06.862
off AD DNS and DHCP onto one policy plane.

3
00:00:06.862 --> 00:00:11.047
Six phases: inventory,
coexistence, migrating authority,

4
00:00:11.047 --> 00:00:14.787
cloud federation,
decommissioning, and hardening.

5
00:00:14.787 --> 00:00:19.800
Each one ends with a rollback point and
a consistency test, not a calendar date.

6
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:23.725
The playbook's durations are planning
estimates; the gates decide.

7
00:00:23.725 --> 00:00:26.700
And every move of authority
runs the same loop.

8
00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:28.662
Lower the TTL well ahead.

9
00:00:28.662 --> 00:00:32.063
Export, transform and
import with a dry run.

10
00:00:32.063 --> 00:00:34.124
Validate from every origin.

11
00:00:34.124 --> 00:00:36.638
Switch authority one mechanism at a time.

12
00:00:36.638 --> 00:00:39.526
Wait until no client
queries the old server.

13
00:00:39.526 --> 00:00:42.713
Then restore the TTL
and file the evidence.

14
00:00:42.713 --> 00:00:45.301
If a check fails, you revert the switch,

15
00:00:45.301 --> 00:00:48.790
and the old authority,
still intact, answers again.
